[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Tutorial: Mocking Static Methods in Mockito"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Prior to Mockito 3.4.0, mocking static methods required complex workarounds or third-party byte-code manipulation libraries like PowerMock. With the introduction of Mockito's inline mocking feature, you can now mock static methods natively using 'MockedStatic'."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Ensure you are using Mockito version 3.4.0 or higher. For Gradle or Maven, use the 'mockito-inline' dependency, or rely on the standard 'mockito-core' if you are on Mockito 4.0.0+ where the inline mock maker is enabled by default."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding MockedStatic"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"The core component for static mocking is the 'MockedStatic' interface. Because static methods belong to the class rather than an instance, the mock must be scoped tightly, typically using a Java 'try-with-resources' block to ensure the static mock is deregistered after the test executes."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Code Example: Mocking a Static Method"},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"public class MathUtils {
    public static int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }
}

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.mockito.MockedStatic;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;
import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;

public class MathUtilsTest {
    @Test
    public void testStaticMethod() {
        try (MockedStatic<MathUtils> mockedMath = mockStatic(MathUtils.class)) {
            mockedMath.when(() -> MathUtils.add(2, 3)).thenReturn(10);

            int result = MathUtils.add(2, 3);

            assertEquals(10, result);
        }
    }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always use try-with-resources with 'MockedStatic' to avoid contaminating other tests."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep static method mocking to a minimum. Heavy reliance on static methods usually indicates tightly coupled legacy code that would benefit from dependency injection."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Verify static calls explicitly using 'mockedMath.verify(() -> MathUtils.add(2, 3), times(1))'."}]
